body:json {
  {
    "plan_id": 1
  }
}

docs {
  # Submit Subscription Request

  The "Buy" button on the plans screen. Files a request for the administrator,
  who gets in touch, settles the payment and approves or rejects it. Nothing is
  granted until then.

  Runs on the plain client token (`ensure.client`): open to masters — including
  ones whose access has already run out — and to ordinary clients alike. The
  administrator can only approve a request from an **approved** master profile.

  **Request:**

  | Field     | Type    | Required | Description                                          |
  |-----------|---------|----------|------------------------------------------------------|
  | `plan_id` | integer | yes      | `id` from `GET /api/v1/master/subscription-plans`    |

  **Response 201:**
  ```json
  {
    "message": "Заявка отправлена. Администратор свяжется с вами",
    "data": {
      "id": 42,
      "plan_id": 1,
      "plan_name": "1 месяц",
      "price": 1250,
      "duration_days": 30,
      "status": "pending",
      "status_label": "Ожидает",
      "rejection_reason": null,
      "reviewed_at": null,
      "created_at": "2026-10-09T12:00:00+05:00"
    }
  }
  ```

  `status`: `pending` / `approved` / `rejected`.

  **After review** a push arrives with `data.type`:
  - `subscription_request.approved` — also `subscription_request_id`, `subscription_id`
  - `subscription_request.rejected` — also `subscription_request_id`; the body is the reason when one was given

  Both carry `audience: master`.

  **Errors:**
  - `401` — no token
  - `403` — token is not a client token
  - `409` — the account already has a `pending` request (one at a time, any plan)
  - `422` — `plan_id` missing, not an integer, unknown, disabled or deleted (`errors.plan_id`)
}
